  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of education opportunities and improved access to life saving water, sanitation and hygiene services to the most vulnerable in Marib and Sa&#x2019;ada.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide education and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) to vulnerable communities affected by flood and conflict. This UNICEF project provides access to quality, safe and inclusive learning opportunities for children in affected communities, and also aims to reduce incidences of WASH related diseases and improve the quality of life for children and women in flood and conflict prone areas by providing WASH interventions. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 6,034 people, including 24 women, 50 men, 5,960 children, and including 596 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
